 keeping their  murderous intense suppressed and hidden  with all this in mind one of Wednesday's  classmates at the Nevermore Academy  quick becomes suspect number one in the  search for its serial killer as the  saying goes it really is always the  quiet ones lots of the students at  Nevermore are just as gloomy or strange  as Wednesday but one of the few normies  Wednesday becomes attached to is Tyler  Galpin the chatty Barista who becomes  smitten with the gothic schoolgirl Tyler  is sweet caring and seems the sort that  wouldn't hurt a fly a real Jekyll type  you might say with that in mind of  course he's hiding a beastly secret in  the form of a seven foot tall feral  creature he can't contain the big  difference between Tyler and the good  doctor from Stevenson's book is that  Tyler doesn't create his vicious Alter  Ego in an experiment he carries his  curse thanks to his family heritage even  so this split between man and monster  still lines up with its inspiration the  dead giveaway nature of the creature's  name likely explains why Wednesday  doesn't uncover what it's called until  pretty late in the series when she even  notes its literary origin it's called a  hide  isn't Jekyll and Hyde unfortunately the  damage Tyler and flicks leaves its mark  his mild Maynard side is eventually  subsumed by his horrific nature and he  becomes like the creature even in his  human form if Wednesday gets a second  season you might expect the love that  could have been for our heroine manifest  as an unhinged enemy who comes back for  Revenge honestly High School romances  really are nothing but trouble
 

